  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "VRChat should offer world creators and prefab creators a way to override VRChat-specific actions bound to certain keys/controls in Udon.\nFor example, I am using a text chat prefab in my world. When players using the chat prefab type messages with their keyboards, pressing certain keys such as C, Z, V, or R causes them to crouch, prone, open their mic or open the action menu respectively. That can be an annoyance to desktop users who want to type without having to change their locomotion state or close the action menu by pressing those keys again. \nIf creators are given the opportunity to override VRC actions bound to certain keys/controls in Udon, then this will allow players to use certain prefabs that require inputting text on their keyboards without triggering specific actions in VRChat when typing certain keys.\nThis request should not be limited to only desktop players. VRC can offer world creators an opportunity to override actions assigned to certain buttons or controls when using VR controllers.",
